===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|operations}} The [[stock]] of an [[item]] on hand at a particular location or business.
#: {{ux|en|Due to an undersized '''inventory''' at the Boston outlet, customers had to travel to Providence to find the item.}}
# {{lb|en|operations}} A detailed [[list]] of all of the items [[on hand]].
#: {{ux|en|The '''inventory''' included several items that one wouldn't normally think to find at a cheese shop.}}
# {{lb|en|operations}} The process of producing or updating such a list.
#: {{ux|en|This month's '''inventory''' took nearly three days.}}
# A space containing the {{l|en|item|items}} available to a character, especially that in a [[video game]], for immediate use.
#: {{ux|en|You can't get through the underground tunnel if there are more than three items in your '''inventory'''.}}
# {{lb|en|linguistics|especially|phonology}} The [[total]] [[set]] of a {{gloss|specified}} linguistic feature {{gloss|within a language etc.}}
#: {{ux|en|Germanic languages have a marked tendency towards  large vocalic '''inventories'''.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2014|editor=Jackson Sun|author=Guillaume Jacques|title=Phonological Profiles of Little-Studied Tibetic Varieties|chapter=V: Cone|location=Taipei|publisher=w:Academia Sinica|page=270|oclc=907654712|isbn=9789860423211|passage=Most final consonants have been lost, resulting in a tonal language with a rich consonantal and vocalic '''inventory''', but with a relatively simple syllabic structure..}}

